'''Cristiano Hamamoto-Sandoval''' (born 14 December 1963) is a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] politician who served as the 41st [[Secretary General of Balisca|Secretary General]] from 2007 to 2019. Sandoval was re-appointed to his position for three consecutive mandates, resulting in a [[Premiership of Cristiano Sandoval|twelve year-long tenure]]. He was the second Secretary General to come from the [[Reformist Bloc (Balisca)|Reformist Bloc]], serving as the organization chairperson from 1997 to 2018. Born to [[Takamaikan Baliscans|Takamaikan immigrants]] to [[Araucaria]], he became the first Secretary General of [[Asian Baliscans|East Asian-Baliscan]] descent.

During the tenure of Sandoval the Confederal Congress ratified the [[2008 Ecology Initiative|Ecology Initiative]] of 2008, condemned the [[W:Iraq War|American-led invasion of Iraq]] and [[W:War on Terror|War on Terror]], and launched an international campaign in support of [[W:Drug liberalization|drug liberalization]] against the destructive [[W:War on Drugs|War on Drugs]]. His administration redoubled Balisca's efforts to achieve {{W|Reform of the UNSC|reform of the UNSC}} (especially regarding a permanent seat for itself). Balisca expanded its ties to {{W|Africa}}, signed the {{W|Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons}}, and entered Balisca into the {{W|Paris Agreement}}.

